WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.950
- [Interviewer] All right Bob.

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.110
- Yes.
- Bob, where'd you grow up?

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.160
Where are you from originally?

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.023
- [Bob] I'm originally
from Brooklyn, New York.

00:00:07.023 --> 00:00:08.280
- [Interviewer] And tell
me about your childhood.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.620
You had both your parents
when you were a kid?

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.410
- [Bob] No, I was raised
by my grandparents.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.953
- [Interviewer] What
happened to mom and dad?

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:20.040
- Didn't like each other
so my granddad took me.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.113
They divorced.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.543
My parents divorced and I
wound up with my grandparents.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.560
- [Interviewer] How would
you describe your childhood?

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.110
- Okay.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:30.943
Okay.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.580
- [Interviewer] Nothing
going on that was awful?

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.363
- Not until I turned 17,

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.343
and then I went off to Vietnam.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.420
- [Interviewer] Tell me about Vietnam.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.947
- Not much fun. It was not a good thing.

00:00:48.947 --> 00:00:50.453
No, it was not a good thing.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:53.933
No.

00:00:55.103 --> 00:00:55.936
- [Interviewer] What did you do

00:00:55.936 --> 00:00:57.400
after you came back from Vietnam?

00:00:58.354 --> 00:01:00.104
- I lived here. I moved right here.

00:01:01.034 --> 00:01:05.133
And then I worked on the oil platforms

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:07.963
most of my life.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:12.533
And,

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:17.240
I've got a daughter and two grandkids,

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:20.103
and I give them my retirement.

00:01:23.938 --> 00:01:24.771
- [Interviewer] And you've been living

00:01:24.771 --> 00:01:26.160
in the Tenderloin for how long?

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:30.623
- About two years.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:34.420
- [Interviewer] But you've
in the Bay Area since when?

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:39.380
- I moved over there in North beach,

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.010
it's probably 16 years.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.723
17 years.
- But you moved here from-

00:01:42.723 --> 00:01:47.180
- And then I moved up
over the hill to the TL.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.750
- [Interviewer] Okay, but you
lived in the Bay Area since-

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.067
- Oh, 40 years?

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:53.071
- 40 years?
- Yeah, 40.

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:54.426
- [Interviewer] How old are you now?

00:01:54.426 --> 00:01:55.633
- I'm 70.
- 70.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.500
And there's a lot of drugs
here in the Tenderloin.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.563
Has drugs been a part of your life too?

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.040
- Not really.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.053
I stay to myself.

00:02:10.064 --> 00:02:11.005
- [Interviewer] Do you have friends?

00:02:11.005 --> 00:02:12.773
- Yeah, I got a couple.

00:02:12.773 --> 00:02:14.450
- [Interviewer] And you were married once?

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:15.283
- Oh yeah.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.040
Yeah, she passed away about...

00:02:19.886 --> 00:02:20.847
It was five, six years ago.

00:02:20.847 --> 00:02:22.263
- [Interviewer] Oh, I'm sorry.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.310
And looking back at your life,
what regrets do you have?

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:35.303
- Oh, I really don't know.

00:02:35.303 --> 00:02:36.970
I really don't know.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:42.157
I think I've had a fairly
decent life, nothing tragic.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.853
Till my wife died.

00:02:48.789 --> 00:02:50.740
- [Interviewer] You would say
you had a pretty good life?

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.674
- Yeah, I believe so. Yeah.

00:02:52.674 --> 00:02:54.193
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:56.860
- [Interviewer] Are you religious?

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.510
- No, I'm not very religious guy.

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:04.423
- [Interviewer] What's been
the best time of your life?

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.290
- Best time in my life?

00:03:18.537 --> 00:03:19.480
I've had a pretty good life.

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:21.040
I guess when I got married and stuff

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.730
would be about the best time of my life.

00:03:24.757 --> 00:03:25.590
Yeah.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:26.930
- [Interviewer] And what's
been the roughest time?

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.030
Roughest thing you went through.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:30.430
- When my wife got the cancer.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.063
- [Interviewer] Yeah.
Yeah, that would do it.

00:03:37.112 --> 00:03:38.110
What would you say is the most important

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.180
lesson you've learned in your life?

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:41.990
The most important lesson?

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.250
- Not really, I don't know.

00:03:49.827 --> 00:03:54.520
Probably, lesson I've
learned is pretty much

00:03:55.795 --> 00:03:58.243
don't trust anybody.

00:03:58.243 --> 00:03:59.663
- [Interviewer] I hear that a lot.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:04.348
- That's why I was sort of skeptic

00:04:04.348 --> 00:04:07.093
when you first talked to me.

00:04:07.093 --> 00:04:07.926
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:04:07.926 --> 00:04:11.176
It's a strange request from a stranger.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.840
Do you believe in karma?

00:04:15.967 --> 00:04:17.162
- I do.

00:04:17.162 --> 00:04:17.995
Sure.

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:22.090
What goes around comes around.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:23.563
I believe in that for sure.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:28.360
- [Interviewer] And you'd
been in love before.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.507
It sounds like with your wife?

00:04:30.507 --> 00:04:31.580
- Excuse me?

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.133
- [Interviewer] You've
been in love before.

00:04:34.269 --> 00:04:35.512
- Before my wife?

00:04:35.512 --> 00:04:37.375
- [Interviewer] I assume you had.

00:04:37.375 --> 00:04:41.010
